            <div xml:id="d189">

                <pb facs="0280" n="182" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg182"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/5443: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-07-23T18:00:00+08:00">July 23, 1932—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 23—6:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>844. Following from American Consul General at Mukden: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“July 22, 6 p.m. The Japanese detachment which entered Jehol proceeded
                            only as far as Chaoyangsu; according to local
                            official Japanese sources a part of the detachment has withdrawn from
                            Jehol and negotiations for Ishimoto’s release are progressing satisfactorily.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
